Vendor (Ingenic 3.10.14) interfaces for camera drivers ported to Linux 6.18.

t20-compat.c   /proc/jz, jzgpio_set_func(), ispmem_base/size, t20_intc_irq(),
               the tx-isp platform devices (from soc-t20/common/platform.c).
               Builds; not in the image yet (nothing uses it until the ISP
               driver builds).
include/       Vendor headers the drivers include: mach/tx_isp.h and
               media/v4l2-chip-ident.h copied from the 3.10.14 tree, soc/base.h
               (SoC addresses) copied, soc/gpio.h, soc/irq.h, jz_proc.h,
               mach/platform.h written for this layer.

Build (after kernel/build.sh):
  make -C build/kernel/obj M=$PWD/kernel/compat ARCH=mips \
      CROSS_COMPILE=mipsel-linux-gnu- modules

open-tx-isp driver/t20 against 6.18 (2026-10-27, open-tx-isp b4d8eae,
ingenic-sdk 5e5d7d2), with kernel/config's V4L2 and media controller
modules and KCPPFLAGS=-I$PWD/kernel/compat/include (plus an empty
txx-funcs.h in the SDK include directory): 272 errors, by cause:

  - Media bus codes renamed: V4L2_MBUS_FMT_* -> MEDIA_BUS_FMT_* (most of
    the count; tx-isp-core.c, tx-isp-core-tuning.c, tx-isp-vic.c,
    tx-isp-common.h). A table of #defines.
  - Removed V4L2 interfaces: v4l2_subdev_core_ops .g_ctrl/.s_ctrl/
    .g_chip_ident; v4l2_ioctl_ops .vidioc_g/s_ctrl, g/s_priority, g/s_crop,
    cropcap; VFL_TYPE_GRABBER (now VFL_TYPE_VIDEO); V4L2_FL_USE_FH_PRIO;
    video_device.debug; media_device.link_notify (now in media_device_ops);
    media_entity_init/media_entity_create_link (now media_entity_pads_init,
    media_create_pad_link). Controls already use the v4l2_ctrl framework.
  - videobuf2 (tx-isp-frame-channel.c, tx-isp-videobuf.c, the frame
    channels libimp reads): vb2_buffer.v4l2_buf is now vb2_v4l2_buffer,
    vb2_queue.timestamp_type is timestamp_flags, vb2_qbuf() takes a media
    device, and the module's own vb2 memory allocator uses the 3.10
    dma_buf_ops (kmap/kmap_atomic gone, dma_buf_export takes an info
    struct) and sets vma->vm_flags directly (vm_flags_set()). The largest
    piece: the frame channel ABI libimp expects must stay identical.
  - tx-isp-load-parameters.c: mm_segment_t/set_fs/KERNEL_DS and f_dentry
    (kernel_read, f_path.dentry).
  - misc_deregister() returns void (system_chardev.c, tx-isp-debug.c,
    tx-isp-vic.c, tx-isp-core.c).
  - Constants the 3.10 build found through its include order (VIC_*
    registers, TX_ISP_INPUT_PORT_MAX_*, TX_ISP_DS1_CHANNEL_MAX_*,
    TX_ISP_EXIST_FR_CHANNEL, isp_clk): include path, not API.
  - struct timespec on the stack (timespec64).

Not reached yet: link errors (the recovered firmware unit declares kernel
functions with its own prototypes) and the sensor drivers, which use the
same subdev interfaces.
